# 02. History

## 5. PostgreSQL Origins

PostgreSQL has its roots in the **POSTGRES project** at the University of California, Berkeley.

The project was started in the 1980s under the leadership of **Michael Stonebraker**.

The original POSTGRES system was designed to explore improvements beyond traditional relational database systems.

Later, SQL support was added, and the project eventually became known as PostgreSQL.

---

## Important Timeline

A simplified timeline:

```text
1986
 │
 ▼
POSTGRES project
 │
 ▼
Evolution and development
 │
 ▼
SQL support added
 │
 ▼
Postgres95
 │
 ▼
PostgreSQL
 │
 ▼
Modern PostgreSQL
```

The name **PostgreSQL** reflects its origins in POSTGRES while emphasizing its SQL capabilities.

---

# 6. Evolution of PostgreSQL

Over time, PostgreSQL evolved from a research database project into a mature production database system.

Its development expanded to support:

```text
SQL
+
Transactions
+
Indexes
+
Advanced data types
+
JSON
+
JSONB
+
Extensions
+
Replication
+
Performance improvements
```

The important point for this lesson is:

> PostgreSQL wasn't designed as a modern cloud database from day one. It evolved over decades into a powerful general-purpose database.

