# 24. PostgreSQL vs MongoDB

This is an important distinction.

### PostgreSQL

Primarily relational:

```text
Tables
Rows
Columns
Relationships
```

### MongoDB

Document-oriented:

```text
Collections
     ↓
Documents
     ↓
JSON-like structures
```

Conceptually:

```text
PostgreSQL

students
├── id
├── name
└── age
```

versus:

```text
MongoDB

students
{
    "name": "Janusha",
    "age": 28
}
```

### Interview Answer

> PostgreSQL is primarily a relational database using tables and relationships, while MongoDB is a document-oriented NoSQL database that stores flexible document structures. PostgreSQL is generally a strong choice when relational integrity and complex relationships are important.

